# "Target nonland permanent": Bot2's Forest is refused as a target while its Ornithopter (the positive control) is not.
# Then Bot2 sacrifices a Welding Jar in response to give the second Ornithopter a regeneration shield (CR 701.19a): the
# targeted Ornithopter is destroyed, the shielded namesake is only tapped (the destroy of each is its own, CR 701.8, 701.19)
# and the Jar, a different name, is not touched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Maelstrom Pulse
Swamp x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Welding Jar
Welding Jar
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Welding Jar.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Welding Jar.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Maelstrom Pulse.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Hand.Maelstrom Pulse.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Welding Jar.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Ornithopter; Welding Jar
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Welding Jar
Bot1.Graveyard = Maelstrom Pulse
Stack.Count = 0
